Options for these steps

Usage: postgwas pipeline [options] --modules gcta_gene

Options:
  -h, --help              show this help message and exit
  --show-screen           Display PostGWAS progress, summaries, warnings, and
                          errors in the terminal (Default: true).
  --hide-screen           Hide PostGWAS terminal output while continuing to
                          save the same screen stream to
                          logging.screen_log_file.

Performance:
  --threads N             Total CPU-thread budget across all concurrent tasks.
                          PostGWAS chooses automatically if omitted
                          (Default: 11).
  --memory-gb GB          Maximum total memory PostGWAS may use, in gigabytes.
                          If omitted, PostGWAS uses up to 90% of available
                          physical memory (Default: 57 GB).
  --seed N                Number used to make randomized analyses
                          reproducible. Use the same value to reproduce a run
                          (Default: 10).

Run continuation:
  --resume, --no-resume   Reuse existing outputs only after the selected
                          module validates their completion state and
                          provenance (Default: true).
  --overwrite             Replace existing outputs owned by the selected run;
                          this takes precedence over resume (Default: false).

Input file:
  --vcf PATH              Required: Harmonised GWAS-VCF file to analyse.

Output:
  --dataset-id NAME       Required: Short, unique name for the dataset, such
                          as PGC3_SCZ_EUR. It is used in output file names.
  --output-directory PATH
                          Required: Folder where PostGWAS will save results
                          and logs.

Variant identifiers:
  --variant-id-type {rsid,unique}
                          Identifier convention written to every explicitly
                          selected format. Use 'rsid' to extract an rsID from
                          the VCF ID field or 'unique' to construct the
                          configured chromosome-position-REF-ALT identifier.
                          Per-target YAML settings can use different
                          conventions (Default: rsid). Available options:
                          rsid, unique.
  --duplicate-id-policy POLICY
                          Action for conflicting duplicate IDs after
                          collapsing exact repeated records and applying
                          supported reference matching (currently LDSC
                          --merge-alleles). exclude_all removes every
                          ambiguous record; error stops; most_significant,
                          highest_maf, and highest_info retain only a unique
                          best-ranked row. A missing ranking value or tied
                          best rank excludes the whole group. Per-target YAML
                          settings can use different policies
                          (Default: exclude_all). Available options:
                          exclude_all, error, most_significant, highest_maf,
                          highest_info.

External software:
  --bcftools PATH         Full path or command name for bcftools
                          (Default: bcftools).

GCTA association inputs:
  --gcta-reference-prefix PREFIX
                          Prefix shared by the PLINK BED, BIM, and FAM
                          LD-reference files (Default: unset).
  --gene-list PATH        Required: for fastbat_gene, mbat_combo, or
                          fastbat_set with --gmt.
                          Four-column chromosome, start, end, gene-ID file
                          used by GCTA (Default: unset).
  --fastbat-set-list PATH
                          Prepared custom fastBAT set file containing a set
                          ID, SNP IDs, and END. Use this or --gmt, not both
                          (Default: unset).
  --gmt PATH              GMT pathway file converted to a fastBAT set list
                          using --gene-list and the reference BIM; mutually
                          exclusive with --fastbat-set-list (Default: unset).

Input and reference compatibility:
  --genome-build BUILD    Shared genome build of the harmonised GWAS, PLINK LD
                          reference, and gene list when used; all
                          coordinate-bearing inputs must match
                          (Default: unset). Available options: GRCh37, GRCh38.
  --gcta-reference-population CODE
                          Population represented by the LD reference; no
                          ancestry is inferred (Default: unset). Available
                          options: EUR, AFR, EAS, SAS, AMR.

GCTA association settings:
  --method {fastbat_gene,fastbat_segment,fastbat_set,mbat_combo}
                          Choose the tested unit and GCTA procedure:
                          fastbat_gene: Test SNPs assigned to each gene and
                          its configured window with LD-aware fastBAT.
                          fastbat_segment: Test consecutive fixed-size genomic
                          segments with LD-aware fastBAT.
                          fastbat_set: Test custom SNP sets supplied through
                          --fastbat-set-list or converted from --gmt pathways.
                          mbat_combo: Test each gene by combining signed mBAT
                          and unsigned fastBAT evidence
                          (Default: fastbat_gene). Available options:
                          fastbat_gene, fastbat_segment, fastbat_set,
                          mbat_combo.
  --gene-window-kb KB     Window added to both sides of each gene boundary
                          (Default: 50).
  --gmt-chromosome-label-policy {exact,strip_chr_prefix}
                          How GMT conversion reconciles gene-list and BIM
                          chromosome labels (Default: exact). Available
                          options: exact, strip_chr_prefix.
  --gmt-duplicate-gene-policy {error,deduplicate}
                          How repeated gene symbols within a GMT pathway are
                          handled (Default: deduplicate). Available options:
                          error, deduplicate.
  --gmt-unmapped-gene-policy {error,report}
                          Whether GMT genes absent from the coordinate file
                          fail or are reported (Default: report). Available
                          options: error, report.
  --gmt-empty-pathway-policy {error,omit}
                          Whether pathways with no usable variants after
                          BIM/GWAS intersection fail or are omitted
                          (Default: omit). Available options: error, omit.
  --fastbat-oversized-set-policy {error,omit}
                          How sets above GCTA's 20,000-variant hard limit are
                          handled (Default: omit). Available options: error,
                          omit.
  --fastbat-segment-size-kb KB
                          Fixed segment size (Default: 100).
  --gcta-coordinate-fallback, --no-gcta-coordinate-fallback
                          Resolve nonmatching summary-statistic IDs by an
                          unambiguous chromosome, position, and allele-pair
                          match to the PLINK BIM (Default: true).
  --gcta-minimum-reference-overlap FRACTION
                          Minimum fraction of unique pipeline variants that
                          must resolve to exact PLINK BIM IDs (Default: 0.5).
  --gcta-chromosome-label-policy {exact,strip_chr_prefix}
                          How reference and VCF chromosome labels are
                          normalized before compatibility checks
                          (Default: strip_chr_prefix). Available options:
                          exact, strip_chr_prefix.
  --gcta-allow-strand-complement, --no-gcta-allow-strand-complement
                          Allow complementary single-nucleotide allele pairs
                          when only direct ID matching is available
                          (Default: false).
  --gcta-reference-maf-min FRACTION
                          Minimum MAF retained from the LD reference
                          (Default: 0.01).
  --fastbat-ld-cutoff R2  LD r-squared pruning cutoff used by fastBAT
                          (Default: 0.9).
  --mbat-svd-gamma FRACTION
                          Minimum LD variance retained by mBAT principal
                          components (Default: 0.9).
  --frequency-difference-max FRACTION
                          Maximum A1-frequency difference between GWAS and LD
                          reference (Default: 0.2).
  --print-component-p-values, --no-print-component-p-values
                          Include mBAT and fastBAT component p-values
                          (Default: true).
  --write-snpset, --no-write-snpset
                          Write the SNP sets included in the selected fastBAT
                          or mBAT analysis (Default: false).
  --gcta-top-results N    Number of lowest-p-value associations shown in the
                          terminal summary (Default: 10).
  --gcta-nominal-alpha ALPHA
                          Nominal p-value threshold reported for individual
                          associations (Default: 0.05).
  --gcta-reporting-alpha ALPHA
                          Family-wise alpha used only to report the Bonferroni
                          threshold; results are never filtered by this value
                          (Default: 0.05).
  --gcta-fdr-alpha ALPHA  Benjamini-Hochberg false-discovery-rate threshold
                          (Default: 0.05).
  --gcta-p-value-digits N
                          Significant digits used to display association
                          p-values (Default: 4).
  --gcta PATH             GCTA executable path or command name
                          (Default: gcta64).

Configuration:
  --run-config PATH       YAML file containing settings and reference
                          resources for every selected module.

Choose analyses:
  --modules [MODULE ...]  One or more final analyses to run, for example
                          finemap magma pops. Available options:
                          harmonisation, sumstat_filter, annot_ldblock,
                          formatter, imputation, ld_clump, finemap, magma,
                          gcta_cojo, gcta_gene, magmacovar, single_cell, pops,
                          kpops, caldera, flames, heritability, manhattan,
                          qc_summary, mixer, allele_orientation, enrichment.
  --apply-filter          Run quality-control filtering before downstream
                          analyses.
  --apply-imputation      Impute missing summary statistics before downstream
                          analyses.
  --apply-manhattan       Create Manhattan and QQ plots.
  --heritability          Estimate SNP heritability with LDSC.

Workflow examples

Run gene-based mBAT-combo:
  postgwas pipeline \
    --modules gcta_gene \
    --method mbat_combo \
    --vcf study.vcf.gz \
    --gcta-reference-prefix reference/1000G_EUR \
    --gene-list genes_grch37.txt \
    --genome-build GRCh37 \
    --gcta-reference-population EUR \
    --dataset-id STUDY \
    --output-directory results

Convert a GMT pathway file and run custom-set fastBAT:
  postgwas pipeline \
    --modules gcta_gene \
    --method fastbat_set \
    --vcf study.vcf.gz \
    --gcta-reference-prefix reference/1000G_EUR \
    --gene-list genes_grch37.txt \
    --gmt pathways.gmt \
    --genome-build GRCh37 \
    --gcta-reference-population EUR \
    --dataset-id STUDY \
    --output-directory results

Export a complete configuration for these analyses:
  postgwas config export \
    --pipeline gcta_gene \
    --style full \
    --output analysis_pipeline.yaml

Notes
  The exported configuration includes required preceding modules in execution order.
